// COVERS MongoDBSchemaLexerGrammar: Database, Collection, include, jsonSchema, validationLevel, validationAction, strict, moderate, error, warn, Join, true, false, null
// COVERS MongoDBConnectionLexerGrammar: store, serverURLs, database, debug, authentication
// COVERS MongoDBMappingLexerGrammar: ~filter, ~mainCollection, ~binding, ~distinct, ~primaryKey
//
// All three MongoDB sub-grammars in one file: the ###MongoDB store, the ###Mapping class
// mapping body, and the ###Connection element.
//
// MongoDBSchemaLexerGrammar imports M3LexerGrammar and adds its OWN `QUOTED_STRING` on
// DOUBLE quotes, because the `jsonSchema:` body is literal JSON handed to Jackson. So in
// this section a double-quoted string is the string form and `true`/`false`/`null` are the
// JSON literal tokens -- that is the only place those three keywords are typeable.
// The JSON is deserialized by MongoDBSchemaDeserializer at PARSE time (the walker calls it
// from getSchemaExpression), so it must be a real object schema: `"bsonType": "object"` is
// mandatory or the walker throws "Expected jsonSchema bsonType should be of object type".
// Unrecognised keys are ignored, which is where the `null` sits.
//
// `include` must precede every collection (rule `mongodb` is `include* (collection|join)*`)
// and `Join` is parsed and then dropped -- MongoDBSchemaParseTreeWalker visits only
// ctx.collection(), so a Join has no walker at all. Same for include. Both still have to
// lex and parse, which is what this asserts.
//
// MongoDBMappingLexerGrammar declares five `~` commands but only three are consumed as
// commands: `~filter`, `~mainCollection`, `~binding`. `~distinct` and `~primaryKey` appear
// in no rule except the `unquotedIdentifier` alternation, so the sole way to type them is
// as an identifier -- the filter name and the main-collection name below. They are not
// dead (a rule does reach them) but they carry no meaning.
//
// MongoDBConnectionLexerGrammar's `debug` is the same story: DEBUG is only in
// `unquotedIdentifier`, so it is typeable as the `database:` value and nowhere else.
// `serverURLs` entries are `HOST_STRING COLON INTEGER` -- an unquoted host, no quotes.
###MongoDB
Database fixture::mongo::PersonDb
(
  include fixture::mongo::BaseDb

  Collection Person
  (
    validationLevel: strict;
    validationAction: error;
    jsonSchema: {
      "bsonType": "object",
      "title": "Record of Person",
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "bsonType": "string",
          "description": "name of the person",
          "minLength": 2
        },
        "firmId": {
          "bsonType": "objectId"
        }
      },
      "legendFixtureIgnoredKey": null,
      "additionalProperties": false
    };
  )

  Collection "firm-data"
  (
    validationLevel: moderate;
    validationAction: warn;
    jsonSchema: {
      "bsonType": "object",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "bsonType": "objectId"
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": true
    };
  )

  Join PersonFirm (Person.firmId = [fixture::mongo::PersonDb] "firm-data".id)
)


###Mapping
Mapping fixture::mongo::MongoMapping
(
  *fixture::mongo::Person[person_id]: MongoDB
  {
    ~filter [fixture::mongo::PersonDb] activeOnly
    ~mainCollection [fixture::mongo::PersonDb] Person
    ~binding fixture::mongo::PersonBinding
  }

  *fixture::mongo::Firm[firm_id]: MongoDB
  {
    ~filter [fixture::mongo::PersonDb] ~primaryKey
    ~mainCollection [fixture::mongo::PersonDb] ~distinct
    ~binding fixture::mongo::FirmBinding
  }
)


###Connection
MongoDBConnection fixture::mongo::Conn
{
  database: legend_db;
  store: fixture::mongo::PersonDb;
  serverURLs: [localhost:27071, f12345-001.ab.com:27071];
  authentication: # UserPassword {
    username: 'mongo_ro';
    password: SystemPropertiesSecret
    {
      systemPropertyName: 'sys.prop.name';
    };
  }#;
}

MongoDBConnection fixture::mongo::DebugConn
{
  database: debug;
  store: fixture::mongo::PersonDb;
  serverURLs: [myhost.example.com:27017];
  authentication: # Kerberos {
  }#;
}
